Crystallizer is intended to turn runtime-facing classes, interfaces, and related
type surfaces into exportable structural descriptions.

The design goal is AI-first and tooling-friendly serialization rather than
human-authored prose alone. The layer is meant to help a caller take the shape
of a system that was already built in code and export that shape in formats that
other tools can consume without re-inspecting the original Python objects.

Current direction:
- support structured text exports such as JSON and YAML first
- leave room for later database-backed export targets if that becomes useful

This file is directional project context, not an implementation contract.
